<title>SRI LANKA: Colombo foreign exchange market closed for holiday.</title>
<headline>Colombo foreign exchange market closed for holiday.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka's foreign exchange market is closed on Wednesday for a Buddhist holiday. The market will reopen on Thursday.</p>
<p>The Sri Lankan rupee closed higher against the dollar on Tuesday after the Central Bank set its rupee rates higher against the dollar for the second day in a row.</p>
<p>The rupee ended at 55.53 to the dollar on Tuesday after opening at 55.70.</p>
<p>-- Colombo newsroom 941-434319</p>
